00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:56.803
I know Melissa won't
have a jar like that.

00:03:56.869 --> 00:04:00.707
May I take the fresh oysters,
the clams, and just a jar?

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:02.775
Because that could
be the secret weapon.

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:03.409
- Do it.

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:03.910
- Yeah?

00:04:03.977 --> 00:04:04.677
- Take it.

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:05.511
- Thanks, bud.

00:04:05.578 --> 00:04:06.346
- Share the love.

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:07.380
- I think I'll become a Mainer.

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:08.781
Now, I've got to cook like one.

00:04:08.848 --> 00:04:11.684
So these little pockets
of magic, fingers crossed,

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:13.586
is going to have the
edge over Melissa.

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:14.454
- All right, cool, man.

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:14.954
- Take care.

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:15.788
Thank you.

00:04:15.855 --> 00:04:17.557
- All right.

